1. Round Robin: Passes requests sequentially down the list: Server 1 $\rightarrow$ Server 2 $\rightarrow$ Server 3 $\rightarrow$ Server 1. Best when all servers have identical hardware specs.2. Weighted Round Robin: Assigns higher request quotas to beefier machines (e.g., a 64-core server gets 4x more requests than a 16-core server).3. Least Connections: Evaluates which server currently has the fewest active open connections and sends the new user there. Ideal for long-lived sessions (e.g., database transactions or WebSockets).4. IP Hash (Source IP Hashing): Hashes the client's IP address to map them consistently to the exact same backend server (a basic form of session persistence).5. Least Response Time: Directs traffic to the server with the lowest latency and fewest active requests combined.
